              ]
            }
          ],
          "orig": "Strategic Reserves are forces that one or both players have chosen not to deploy at the start of the battle. These rules explain how to place units into Strategic Reserves, as well as how and when they arrive on the battlefield.",
          "text": "Strategic Reserves are forces that one or both players have chosen not to deploy at the start of the battle. These rules explain how to place units into Strategic Reserves, as well as how and when they arrive on the battlefield."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "refs": [
        "#/texts/1109"
      ],
      "style": "p",
      "source_nodes": [
        {
          "self_ref": "#/texts/1109",
          "parent": {
            "$ref": "#/body"
          },
          "children": [],
          "content_layer": "body",
          "label": "text",
          "prov": [
            {
              "page_no": 43,
              "bbox": {
                "l": 153.0708,
                "t": 628.3682,
                "r": 332.8415500000001,
                "b": 540.8524836198181,
                "coord_origin": "BOTTOMLEFT"
              },
              "charspan": [
                0,
                463
              ]
            }
          ],
          "orig": "These rules let you place units into Strategic Reserves - a special type of Reserves you can use to keep units off the battlefield until you require them. Note that while all Strategic Reserves units are also technically Reserves units, the reverse is not true, and so these rules do not apply to units that are using other rules that enable them to start the battle in Reserves (e.g. Deep Strike). Such units are instead set up as described by those other rules.",
          "text": "These rules let you place units into Strategic Reserves - a special type of Reserves you can use to keep units off the battlefield until you require them. Note that while all Strategic Reserves units are also technically Reserves units, the reverse is not true, and so these rules do not apply to units that are using other rules that enable them to start the battle in Reserves (e.g. Deep Strike). Such units are instead set up as described by those other rules."
        }
      ]
    },
